WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 6: People and Work.

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.860
In this unit the focus is on people and work.

3
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.220
You will explore the many different jobs and
professions that keep communities running,

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.900
from physicians and lawyers to food vendors and commentators.

5
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.440
You will learn how people choose their
careers, what skills different jobs require,

6
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:26.240
and how the world of work connects to ideas of
fairness, justice, and community responsibility.

7
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.100
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.940
By the end of this unit, you will be able to identify
and describe a range of professions and career paths,

9
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.960
explaining the skills and training each one requires.

10
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:47.560
You will also explain how personal interests
and strengths can guide career choices.

11
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:55.000
You will also read a passage about careers and jobs and
answer comprehension questions at different thinking levels.

12
00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.740
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:05.900
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: advertisement,
argumentation, classification, connective, thus,

14
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:06.720
undoubtedly.

15
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.620
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.180
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.380
The reading sequence includes The People Who Keep
a Community Running and Four Professions, One Town.

18
00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:23.760
Read actively.

19
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.440
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.440
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:39.120
The first language focus is Compound
Nouns: Closed, Hyphenated and Open Forms.

22
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:44.780
A compound noun joins two or more words to
make one noun with a single, specific meaning,

23
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.800
and English writes these compounds in three different forms.

24
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:55.000
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.767
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Career Interview Role-Play.

26
00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:05.680
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.260
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.560
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:13.960
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:20.180
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.780
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:29.920
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
